GC_LobbyGameMode : "{A79C4E0A43DEB821}Prefabs/MP/Modes/GC_LobbyGameMode.et" {
 ID "6B100ACBDE90429F"
 components {
  GC_LobbyManager "{6A137A39106A4973}" {
   m_aMissionEvents + {
    GC_Event "{BE0004FA4B79D1FE}" {
     m_sName "Time Limit (event 3, 4800s)"
     m_Advanced GC_EventOptions "{208F2020A0000997}" {
      m_fDelay 4800
     }
     m_aActions {
      GC_MessageAction "{F8DEF7DF005447E1}" {
       m_sTitle "Time Limit Reached - USSR Victory"
       m_sMessage "US was unable to conduct their breach in time."
      }
     }
    }
   }
   m_aBriefings {
    GC_Briefing "{D864C075A5BF735C}" {
     m_iOrder 0
     m_sTitle "REFERENCE POINT"
     m_sContent "RP100 - Key Small Hill - Front Right 500 m "\
     "RP101 - Eastern Edge of Open Field - Front Right 270 m"\
     "RP102 - Western Edge of Open Field - Front Left 300 m "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{1D101E2932A5F129}" {
     m_iOrder 1
     m_sTitle "TIME, WEATHER & TERRAIN"
     m_sContent "a. Time & Weather"\
     "Time:  06:45 (Sunrise)"\
     "Weather: Good Visibility, Clear Day, No Recent Precipitation or Expected"\
     ""\
     "b. Terrain"\
     "Obstacles: ENY has deployed canalizing minefields west and east of the objective. North of OBJ Hill by ~100m, an obstacle has been deployed formed by 3 rows of triple concertina wire. The obstacle is 10 meters in depth with accompanied AP/AT mines."\
     ""\
     "Avenues of Approach:  Primary avenue of approach is from the north in order to avoid ENY western and eastern minefields. The approach has undulating terrain providing pockets of dead ground. "\
     ""\
     "Key Terrain: Hill 35 occupied by ENY is decisive terrain as its control is vital to missions success. A small hill (0391 0131) to the southwest of our assembly area, provides good overwatch for any COY maneuvers east of that position."\
     ""\
     "Field of Observation: The ENY has almost unobstructed sightlines up to DT Romeo West of TRP1. The ENY's observation is blocked to the North East by uncontinuous and sporadic sparse treelines, estimated visibility to the North East is 600m from the ENY position. COY can travel unobserved up to the PLD (purple PL)."\
     ""\
     "Cover and Concealment: Small shrubs will provide concealment and undulating terrain throughout the AO will provide sporadic cover."\
     ""\
     " "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{4856C7D3C1F0D9F4}" {
     m_iOrder 2
     m_sTitle "ENEMY"
     m_sContent "Enemy forces in the region consist of US motorized and mechanized troops with M113. Yesterday, US forces were probing our lines and identifying our minefield edge. We are expecting an assault today, we are confident that Americans will not be able to utilize their vehicles. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{A4511DDA1D14D875}" {
     m_iOrder 3
     m_sTitle "1. SITUATION"
     m_sContent "a. Enemy Forces"\
     "A Platoon of Russian dismounted motor rifle regulars, entrenched in  a well prepared trench position with bunkers, indirect shelters and possibly a fall back trench. ENY has mined and placed fields to CANALIZE approaching elements."\
     ""\
     "b. Friendly Forces"\
     "- Our Company is assembly at area STEEL 0437 0147 "\
     "- BTN ARTY B9 is located at 033 035"\
     "- Neighboring friendly elements maintain sector security but cannot provide immediate direct fire support inside the objective area."\
     ""\
     "c. Attachments / Detachments"\
     "- An Engineering Squad (1'4) has been attached to First Platoon to aid in breach of obstacles. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{907B11186F31FF9A}" {
     m_iOrder 4
     m_sTitle "HIGHER AND ADJACENT"
     m_sContent "221 our platoon has been tasked with holding the trench. Adjacent platoons from our company are holding our flanks. Higher expects this line to maintain control of Torske and ultimately the river."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{FDA92A3D6BBB4188}" {
     m_iOrder 5
     m_sTitle "2. MISSION"
     m_sContent "Bravo Company will SEIZE OBJ HILL NLT than 0800."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{8E7927282CD0B83D}" {
     m_iOrder 6
     m_sTitle "MISSION"
     m_sContent "221 task is to hold the hill to the last man. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{7067949D12E48BD5}" {
     m_iOrder 7
     m_sTitle "3. EXECUTION"
     m_sContent "As per Commander's Intent"\
     ""\
     "Artillery to suppress and provide concealment for Engineering Team to bridge a breach through ENY OBSTACLE IOT allow Bravo Company to Seize OBJ HILL "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{4A0CEDD62E7DE205}" {
     m_iOrder 8
     m_sTitle "ORDER"
     m_sContent "Friendly Mines placed to deny enemy flanking, Three Rows of Triple Strand Concertina with AP Mines 70 m in front of the trench and Concertina Wire around Fallback Trench"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "USSR"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{F3E4FEA250A4B3C7}" {
     m_iOrder 9
     m_sTitle "4. SERVICE SUPPORT"
     m_sContent "a. Logistics"\
     ""\
     "Ammo: Excess Ammunition available in All Squad M113s (Get some ammo you'll be shooting)"\
     ""\
     "M777 PLT(-): 2x Guns. Per Tube: 30x HE, 60x SMK"\
     ""\
     "Explosives: 15x Bangalore in Engineer's M113 , PLT Cmdrs' M113s"\
     ""\
     "Medical: On-site CLS."\
     ""\
     "Recovery: No vehicle recovery assets available inside AO."\
     ""\
     "b. Sustainment Notes"\
     ""\
     "Check for sufficient Bangalores to conduct a breach. "
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{26911B6745BFF238}" {
     m_iOrder 10
     m_sTitle "5. COMMAND & SIGNAL"
     m_sContent "a. Command"\
     ""\
     "COY COMMANDER - Bulldog 6"\
     ""\
     "Succession: Bulldog 7 --> Bulldog 1'6 --> Bulldog 2'6"\
     ""\
     "b. Signal"\
     ""\
     "BULLDOG COY Net: CH48 Mhz"\
     "BULLDOG FIRES NET: CH50 Mhz"\
     "BULLDOG 1st PLT: CH 48.5 Mhz"\
     "BULLDOG 2nd PLT: CH 49 Mhz"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{1315817D80410086}" {
     m_iOrder 11
     m_sTitle "6. BANGLORE USAGE"
     m_sContent "To deploy the Bangalore:"\
     ""\
     "1. Place a Bangalore the same way you place Demo Charges by Equipping it through your hotbar or on any primary weapons slot and left clicking at the correct position."\
     ""\
     "2. When you’re near a placed Bangalore, a “Push” action will appear, hold F (Note: You must have bangalores in your inventory to do so)."\
     ""\
     "3. Each push will extend the Bangalore by adding a new section in front of the previous one. Continue deploying sections until the obstacle is fully bridged."\
     ""\
     "4. Once the full length of the Bangalore has been deployed, you can detonate it using either a timed fuse or a clacker on the first section you placed."\
     "Limitation: Only 6 Bangalores maximum . (Each Bangalore is 1.5 m in Length)"\
     ""\
     "To breach this trench you will need to utilize 6 bangalore . Further recommend doing 6 side by side. "\
     ""\
     "IF BANGALORE IS BUGGED WHEN YOU REACH THE WIRE CALL GM"
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{1856F014332D6EC0}" {
     m_iOrder 12
     m_sTitle "7. M777 USAGE"
     m_sContent "To use the M777:"\
     ""\
     "1. Find out charges and elevation from the ballistic manual."\
     ""\
     "2. Before loading, make sure the gun elevation is below 800, the loading tray is raised, and the breech is open."\
     ""\
     "3. Take a shell from the crate, place it onto the tray, then lower the tray and ram the shell. Raise the tray."\
     ""\
     "4. Take propellant from the crate, look at the breech and load it. Then close the breech."\
     ""\
     "5. On the left side of the howitzer, start aiming (interact, then right click to enter the view). Adjust azimuth and elevation to the target."\
     ""\
     "6. On the right side, fire when ready."\
     ""\
     ""\
     "Other notes:"\
     "- All of the described steps are interactions on the gun. Some might be a bit hard to spot initially."\
     "- If you fire at low angle, be aware there is a chance you'll hit trees if the target isn't elevated (guns do have clearance)."\
     "- Make sure to take an artillery ballistic manual from the crate, the one in your inventory is for mortars."\
     "- If you are doing step 3 for the first time, you may have to slightly move the elevation to be able to place the shell onto the tray."
     m_aFactionKeys {
      "US"
     }
    }
    GC_Briefing "{83E62C63F2ABC99B}" {
     m_iOrder 13
     m_sTitle "Mission Notes"
     m_sContent "<b>Mission Summary:</b>"\
     "US conducts a COY breach of a Soviet mine and wire obstacle to seize a trenchline on Torske Hill. "\
     "PS When you hear the artillery fire take cover."\
     ""\
     "<b>Trench building:</b>"\
     "Trench building time is reduced for the first 5 minutes. Only the AGS Team are permitted to add trenches for the purpose of concealing the AGS and utilizing it. "\
     ""\
     "<b>Map Customizing: </b>"\
     "This mission modifies some of the vegetation and treelines from the original basemap."\
     ""\
     "Green areas indicate locations where new foliage or treelines have been added."\
     ""\
     "<b>Setup timer:</b>"\
     "US: 5 Minutes"\
     ""\
     "<b>End Conditions</b>"\
     "BLUFOR (US) Victory Criteria:"\
     "- Major Victory: USSR attrited to 95% casualties. "\
     ""\
     "OPFOR (USSR) Victory Criteria:"\
     "- Major Victory: US attrited to 90% casualties."\
     "- Minor Victory: US unable to breach obstacle (Time Limit)"\
     ""\
     "<b>Time Limit:</b>"\
     "80 min"\
     ""\
     "GMs are permitted to create a breach in the obstacle for gameplay purposes, if BLUFOR are unable but this will result in automatic defeat for the US."\
     ""\
     "Mission by Blue , Trench by Lancer"\
     "Last updated: 2026-05-06"
    }
   }
  }
 }
}
